@preamble use("time")
sleep
@unchecked
Pauses execution for the specified number of milliseconds.

sleep(ms)

sleep(1000)    # pause for 1 second
sleep(100)     # pause for 100 milliseconds
===
after
Returns a receive-only event channel that produces true once after the
specified number of milliseconds. Unlike sleep, after does not block the
calling process. It is intended to compose with select for timeouts and other
time-based events.

The event is produced once. Sending on the returned channel faults. Ordinary
channels created by channel() remain unbuffered; the timer's internal event
storage is an implementation property and does not introduce general buffered
channels.

after(ms)

let timer = after(0)
recv(timer)    # true
